# =============================================================================
# REDPILLS-range .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Grouped by WHY each pattern is excluded, not just what it matches, so this
# still makes sense to whoever edits it next without re-deriving the reasoning.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output -- written fresh by every episode run, never hand-edited.
# Tracking it means noisy commits on every run and nothing meaningful to diff.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bailey/scenario_gen generated renders -- reproducible on demand from the
# catalog/spec (bailey) or from the current range config (scenario_gen.py).
# Each one embeds a hash/seed of what it was generated from and goes stale the
# moment that source changes -- committing it creates a second source of truth
# that silently drifts, which is exactly what caused this session's stale-file
# bugs (the sysmon_install catalog conflict, the "wq" leftover in a compose
# file nobody meant to commit). Confirmed generated, not hand-authored:
#   - goad-daniel-bailey.yml: bailey's own "GENERATED FILE" header + spec hash
#   - scenario.yml: scenario_gen.py's own docstring names this as its output
#   - topology*.yml: bailey `gen`'s topology output (decided not useful to
#     keep for this project -- drop both the dated and undated copies)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
goad-daniel-bailey.yml
scenario.yml
topology.yml
topology.*.yml
range-config.*.yml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pre-bailey legacy configs -- hand-authored before the catalog/spec/generator
# system existed (confirmed against an August chat where this content was
# built by hand: eng-jump pivot, eng-hmi, the VLAN 10->20->30 network rules).
# Superseded by bailey's catalog + spec. Keep a copy in archive/ outside the
# active config path if you want the history; don't track at the repo root.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
goad-daniel-range.yml
goad-daniel-range-final.yml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries and anything that gets fetched fresh at provision time -- git
# handles these as opaque blobs (no diffs, repo bloats every revision), and
# some of it is sensitive offensive tooling that shouldn't sit in history.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVEs/
*.zip
*.enc
/opt/vulhub/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets -- never belong in git, even as "example" values. Jenkins credential
# store / vault / local .env is the only place these live.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
*_password.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary junk
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.swp